  "scope": "Core inspect_record_recovery owns complete stored-effect admission order after native header reads: bounded image, canonical sequence, identity, deadline, owner, state, optional completed receipt, successor proof, then original key/payload transfer into RecoveryRecord. The real SQLite load loop uses this entry before CheckpointRecovery insertion. Twenty-four database states from eight flow forms yield 49 original records and 784 frozen comparisons, preserving native faults and all metadata/effect/dispatch/group/branch tables. Pending records retain lazy receipt behavior; malformed unused terminal bytes do not cause eager decoding. Native consumers cover noncomparable move-only GUI-local owners, an unsized host, both states, each reached native refusal and unwind, explicit cleanup before callback return construction, and late-proof/commit failure without partial checkpoint publication. Callback-internal side effects and cleanup remain trusted host work, not framework rollback. SQL/codec bounds, original frames/budgets/authority, global graph/reservation checks, watermark validation and final atomic commit remain adapter-owned. No wire/schema change, fuel, evaluator, dispatch, complete native durable VM or repository extraction is introduced.",
